From: steamac <steamac@fxgam.es>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] kk: reject graphics pipelines without input assembly state (mesh)

STEAMAC-CG/CH (1.9.15, M4 Pro, Final Fantasy VII Rebirth 2909400): SIGSEGV
at kk_gather_program+724 (ldrb w0, [x8], x8 = state->ia = NULL) <-
kk_compile_shaders+672 under vkCreateGraphicsPipelines, right after
"kk: mesh shader uses set 1 binding 1 that the pipeline layout does not
provide". KosmicKrisp exposes no mesh or task shading, but 0092 accepts a
mesh stage in place of a vertex shader, and mesh pipelines have no input
assembly state, which gather_graphics_pipeline_create_info (and the VS key
and lowering) read for the topology.

kk_compile_shaders rejects graphics pipelines with mesh or task stages, or
without input assembly state, before any IA use: it logs the stages and
fails creation with VK_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER_NV. No topology is invented.

Regression: REPRO_CASE=sentry-cg-mesh: a mesh + fragment pipeline faults the
1.9.15 driver at kk_gather_program+724 <- kk_compile_shaders+672, the
reported frames; with this patch its creation fails cleanly.

Generated-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index f031971..227392a 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -2871,6 +2871,36 @@ kk_check_color_attachment_formats(struct kk_device *dev,
    return VK_SUCCESS;
 }
 
+/* KosmicKrisp has no mesh or task shading (VK_EXT_mesh_shader is not
+ * exposed), and its graphics programs take the topology from the input
+ * assembly state, which mesh pipelines do not have. Common pipeline
+ * creation (0092) accepts a mesh stage in place of a vertex shader, so a mesh
+ * pipeline reached kk_gather_program with state->ia NULL (STEAMAC-CG/CH,
+ * Final Fantasy VII Rebirth: SIGSEGV reading ia->primitive_topology). Fail
+ * its creation instead. */
+static VkResult
+kk_check_graphics_stages(struct kk_device *dev, uint32_t shader_count,
+                         const struct vk_shader_compile_info *infos,
+                         const struct vk_graphics_pipeline_state *state)
+{
+   if (shader_count == 0 || infos[0].nir->info.stage == MESA_SHADER_COMPUTE)
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   uint32_t stages = 0u;
+   for (uint32_t i = 0u; i < shader_count; ++i)
+      stages |= BITFIELD_BIT(infos[i].nir->info.stage);
+   const bool unsupported =
+      stages & (BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_MESH) | BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_TASK));
+   if (!unsupported && state != NULL && state->ia != NULL)
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   mesa_loge("kk: graphics pipeline rejected: stages 0x%x (%s%s), input assembly "
+             "state %s",
+             stages, (stages & BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_MESH)) ? "mesh " : "",
+             (stages & BITFIELD_BIT(MESA_SHADER_TASK)) ? "task " : "",
+             state == NULL ? "unknown (no pipeline state)"
+                           : state->ia == NULL ? "absent" : "present");
+   return vk_error(dev, VK_ERROR_INVALID_SHADER_NV);
+}
+
 static VkResult
 kk_compile_shaders(struct vk_device *device, uint32_t shader_count,
                    struct vk_shader_compile_info *infos,
@@ -2881,7 +2911,9 @@ kk_compile_shaders(struct vk_device *device, uint32_t shader_count,
 {
    struct kk_device *dev = container_of(device, struct kk_device, vk);
    struct kk_physical_device *pdev = kk_device_physical(dev);
-   VkResult checked = kk_check_color_attachment_formats(dev, state);
+   VkResult checked = kk_check_graphics_stages(dev, shader_count, infos, state);
+   if (checked == VK_SUCCESS)
+      checked = kk_check_color_attachment_formats(dev, state);
    if (checked != VK_SUCCESS) {
       for (uint32_t i = 0u; i < shader_count; ++i)
          ralloc_free(infos[i].nir);
